title The door that was already right
prompt Autonomous loop -- roster cold first, Standfast on reds, next agent-doable lap Lindy-first crux-first, rota row N mod 5, send each finished increment, seed cadence on the closing lap
think Lap index from git rev-list --count HEAD = 3370, so the council rota reads row 3370 mod 5 = 0 -- Aether and Jupiter, why the work exists. Follow-our-compass, the-lindy-effect-and-the-long-return, and the-grain-and-the-crossing. The Lindy foundation governed this lap in one sentence: a README is the most Lindy-exposed artifact a project owns, read first and cited most. That is what the whole front-door arc was for, and this lap closed its last door.
think 3370 mod 5 == 0 also makes this the seed cadence lap. ITINERARY resolves the conflict between the cadence and the custody gates for itself: run the projection and the four gates, which are agent-doable, and surface the force-push rather than reading the grant in my own favour. Precedent 20260823.142302.
think The previous lap's recommend named constel/README.md and asked for the named-against-standing count first, as the last two laps did. It came back 31 of 31 -- every module named, every tools/f/fora_*_witness.rish path named and correct, and the highest rung cited (FORA30) matching the highest on disk. That is the answer that made this round different from the four before it: no miscount to repair.
think So the fault was length alone: 69,979 bytes over 109 lines. Two blocks carried nearly all of it -- one 9,848-byte sentence under The road on, accreted `and now...` rung by rung across thirty rungs and still opening with its FORA10-vintage summary, and a 4,558-byte Kin: line chaining twenty-three design notes. The Status: line recited all thirty-one rungs inline.
think That makes constel_module_roster the first roster guard in the tree seated as prevention rather than repair. The four before it were each booked by a page already wrong -- 73 of 110 (%184), 112 of 227 (%189), 83 of 240 (%190) -- or by a guard that was right and off the roster (%191). Seating one over a directory that is correct today is the only time it costs nothing and buys the whole of what it is for.
think The split moved the rung sections, the prove block, the road-on narrative, the rung recital and the kin chain word for word, verified by diff against the departing slices rather than by reading them over. The Door page came out at 4,079 bytes, in family with 3,977 (Lotus), 4,444 (Crypto), and 6,928 (Open Image).
think The DOOR meter then read my own new page at 47% against a 20% ceiling -- the highest opening reading of the five, and honestly so: this module's entire subject is a refusal, that a name can never be a real ship. It swept to 5% with every claim held exactly. The missing vowel keeps its name, in the one sentence the meter still counts and in the benediction, because that is what the property is called.
think The cold roster opened at 47 guards, 45 green, 2 red -- tracked_link and readme_reach. tracked_link went green the moment the new pages were staged, which is the untracked shape it exists to catch. readme_reach stayed red, and its root was mine.
think Booking %192 carried the REDS pin to 25,348 bytes over its 24,576 bound, so row %190 folded to construction/archive/ -- and the fold moved the row's text without its depth. Five tree links still read ](../lotus/LADDER.md) from one directory further down. readme_reach named all five in its own output, broken_in_living=5, living_files_affected=1, and the repair was one regex that leaves ../REDS.md alone. Second firing of %183's shape, a fold moves depth; that one was a tool and was repaired by fixing the tool, this one is a hand fold and the REDS ledger has no fold tool. The loom already stood.
think construction/ITINERARY.md carried a verbatim 14-line duplicate -- Open, named, and waiting on its own lap plus Two questions answered so a lap need not reopen them, both appearing twice. Confirmed identical by comparing the two slices before cutting, so the card is single-stranded again. It also said five module front doors and then listed six; the card now says six and names all six.
obs A page can be entirely accurate and still past anyone's willingness to read it. Four laps of this arc were repairs of a miscount; this one had no miscount, and the guard is worth exactly as much. Truth that was checked stays checkable, and truth merely asserted decays -- the Lindy foundation's own line, and the reason a correct directory still wants a guard.
obs One scan now serves four directories. image/, lotus/, crypto/, and constel/ are held by tools/fixtures/module_roster_scan.sh, which takes the directory as an argument, so the constel guard adds no scan of its own -- a witness file and nothing more, exactly as the itinerary predicted when it named this page.
obs geode_libraries and readme_metrics both read red on the staged tree, which is the documented pre-commit shape: adding a witness makes both generated pages stale until tools/hooks/pre-commit fires at git commit. Rather than trust the hook to repair them after the roster measured, both were regenerated by hand first, so the hot roster reads the tree the commit actually ships.
loom witness=constel_module_roster modules=31 rows=31 unrostered=0 phantom=0 duplicate=0 mismatched=0 control_cases=16 control_fail=0
