loom roster=standing_equipment guards=47 cold_green=45 cold_red=2
file constel/README.md the Door front page, 69,979 -> 4,079 bytes, swept 47% -> 5% with every claim held
file constel/LADDER.md the thirty-one rung sections, the thirty-one prove commands, the road-on narrative, the rung recital and the kin chain, moved word for word
file constel/MODULES.md 31 rows in eleven families, each sentence read from that module's own //! head and turned plain ASCII
file tools/co/constel_module_roster_witness.rish the 47th standing guard, fourth consumer of one scan, proven RED both ways on the real page
file tools/fixtures/prose_register_scan.sh constel/README.md joins the DOOR roster so a meter reads it
file construction/standing-equipment.kyri constel_module_roster seated 47th
file construction/REDS.md row %192 and the depth slip owned inside it; row %190 folded to keep the pin under bound
file construction/archive/REDS-the-glob-that-was-not-a-path-rows-190.md the folded row, its link depth repaired to ../../
file construction/ITINERARY.md the front-door arc closed at six doors, a verbatim 14-line duplicate cut, 46 guards -> 47
recommend keep-going docs/CRYPTO.md at 69,099 bytes is the last living document past the 24,576-byte bound that a split would serve, and it wants a different answer from the six: a docs-shelf page has no .rye directory beside it, so module_roster_scan.sh reads nothing there and its roster guard has to be drawn rather than reused. Beside it stands the reading this arc measured twice and left open -- no guard reads a Ceiling: header anywhere in the tree, and the one page that declares one drifted past it without a sound.
